# Job activation flags for .github/workflows/lean.yml.
#
# These began as milestone gates for the Lean port and now serve as a kill
# switch for a gate that has grown too expensive to run on every PR.
#
# LEAN_SELFHOST gates the Level 1 sweep. LEAN_SELFHOST_L2 gates the Level 2
# (metacircular) sweep separately. It was OFF because L2 took ~16 minutes of a
# CI run we want to keep under 10, the Zig backend being ~7.5x slower per case
# than the Chez Scheme path it replaced (#385).
#
# Back ON, but for master pushes and the nightly cron only -- not pull requests.
# The jobs in lean.yml run concurrently, so L2 would set the whole run's wall
# clock; keeping it off PRs holds PR feedback at ~3 minutes while still catching
# a regression within a day. Since #395 it had been running nowhere at all,
# which was the actual loss.
#
# L2 is split across jobs: `l2-build` compiles the evaluator once and uploads it,
# and `l2-case` runs one case per job from that artifact. One job running all
# five took 26.7 minutes; this keeps every job under 10. Running a case alone on
# a runner also removes the contention that made five concurrent cases blow past
# the 600s CASE_TIMEOUT, so the budget has more headroom than it did at
# PARALLEL_JOBS=2 (435-492s per case).
#
# #385 closed once L2's per-case ratio against a Chez-based reference came down
# from ~7.5x to ~5x (measured serially on an M-series Mac: 154s vs 31s on Fib).
# That reference backend was removed once #385 closed (#400) -- the git history
# around #385/#400/#404 has the numbers if this ever needs re-measuring.
#
# If a case times out, take the time out of the case (#407) or narrow the
# trigger. Do not raise CASE_TIMEOUT -- that is what buried #385 the first time.
LEAN_ZIG=1
LEAN_SELFHOST=1
LEAN_SELFHOST_L2=1

# NIX_BUILD gates the flake.nix build+smoke-test job. Same reasoning as
# LEAN_SELFHOST_L2 above: a from-source Lean bootstrap (flake.nix pins an
# off-nixpkgs-cache 4.32.0, see PR #421) takes 45-60 minutes with no
# cache.nixos.org substitute, so it also only runs for master pushes and
# the nightly cron, not pull requests (enforced directly in lean.yml's
# job condition, same as LEAN_SELFHOST_L2's).
NIX_BUILD=1
